Hisense A6L r5 review round4 fix F37 (28 Sep 2026) for the AOSP AIDL example audio HAL (ModulePrimary's Telephony):
  - TelecomConfig.voiceVolume (DeviceHalAidl::setVoiceVolume, Android's in-call volume) is applied to the modem call
    downlink through a6l-q6voiced ("volume <0..1>" -> kernel "VoiceMMode1 RX Volume Step", CVP
    VSS_IVOLUME_CMD_SET_STEP, kernel patch kvoice/a6l-q6voice-rx-volume-v75.patch) BEFORE it is cached; a failure is
    returned (EX_ILLEGAL_STATE, EX_UNSUPPORTED_OPERATION when the kernel lacks the control) and the old value kept.
Applied in hardware/interfaces by tools/rom-v2-pipeline.sh (audio/patches/*.patch).

